.TH DDPAR-CHECK 1 "2026-10-17" "ddpar 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ddpar-check \- verify a ddpar backup or clone using SHA256
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ddpar-check
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compare exactly two of source (\-s), backup (\-b) and destination (\-d).
Local backup checks require SHA256 files created by ddpar \-s.
A clone check without \-b compares source and destination directly.
The command is also available as ddpar-check.sh.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-b " base"
Backup basename including its path, without the \-metadata.txt or part suffix.
With remote operation, the backup belongs to the remote host.
.TP
.BI \-s " path"
Local source file or block device.
.TP
.BI \-d " path"
Destination file or block device. With a remote clone check (no \-b),
this path belongs to the remote host; otherwise it is local.
.TP
.BI \-j " number"
Worker count for clone checks (default: 4). Backup checks use metadata.
.TP
.BI \-B " bytes"
Block size for clone checks (default: 1048576). Backup checks use metadata.
.TP
.BR \-r " [n|c]"
Enable remote checking (default: n). Mode n fetches compressed backup parts
via SSH and decompresses locally; mode c decompresses and hashes remotely.
Mode l is rejected.
.TP
.BI \-R " [user@]host"
SSH host or SSH configuration alias. Also enables remote operation.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show built-in help. Unlike ddpar and ddpar-restore, this command has no
\-\-input or \-\-output aliases.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ddpar-check \-s /dev/sdb \-b /mnt/backups/sdb
ddpar-check \-b /mnt/backups/sdb \-d restored.img
ddpar-check \-s source.img \-d clone.img \-j 8
ddpar-check \-s source.img \-d /remote/clone.img \-r \-R user@host
.fi
.SH NOTES
Checks do not write to source, backup or destination. They detect corrupt or
missing parts, invalid lengths and mismatching hashes.
Use the clone's worker count and block size for clone checks.
Remote checks use SSH rather than netcat for the data and hashes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates a matching comparison; nonzero indicates an error or mismatch.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sha256sum (1),
.BR ddpar (1),
.BR ddpar-restore (1)
